window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Complex Analysis", "projects": [{"id": "CA-01", "slug": "cauchy-integral-formula", "title": "Cauchy Integral Formula", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe holomorphic on an open neighborhood of the closed disk\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline{D(z_0,R)}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside the disk, prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∮</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(w)=\\frac1{2\\pi i}\\oint_{|z-z_0|=R}f(z)/(z-w)\\,dz</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith positive orientation.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Holomorphic means complex differentiable on an open neighborhood of\nthe closed disk. Import Cauchy–Goursat in a finitely connected region\nwith piecewise smooth boundary: the positively oriented boundary\nintegral of a holomorphic function is zero. Also use continuity and the\nparametrization of a circle. Inner boundary components carry clockwise\ninduced orientation.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Excise the evaluation point", "proof": "1. Choose ρ>0 so the closed disk about w of radiusρ lies inside D(z₀,R).\n\n2. On the region between the outer circle and this small disk, h(z)=f(z)/(z−w) is holomorphic.\n\n3. Cauchy–Goursat with its induced boundary orientations gives ∮outer h dz−∮|z−w|=ρ h dz=0, where both displayed circles are individually counterclockwise.", "role": "<p>Move the integral to a small circle without crossing a\nsingularity.</p>", "inputs": "<p>w inside disk; f holomorphic near closure; foundational imports\nstated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The outer integral equals the counterclockwise inner integral.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The outer integral equals the counterclockwise inner\nintegral.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain w inside disk; f holomorphic near closure; foundational\nimports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Move the integral to a small circle without crossing a\nsingularity.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The singular point must be removed; the sign of the inner boundary\nmatters.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nso the closed disk about w of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies inside\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(z_{0},R)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>On the region between the outer circle and this small disk,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z)=f(z)/(z-w)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis holomorphic.</p>", "<p>Cauchy–Goursat with its induced boundary orientations gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">outer</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint \\operatorname{outer}</annotation></semantics></math>\nh\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz-\\oint |z-w|=\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nh\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere both displayed circles are individually counterclockwise.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>The singular point must be removed; the sign of the inner boundary\nmatters. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: The singular point must be removed;\nthe sign of the inner boundary matters. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Evaluate the shrinking circle", "proof": "1. Split f(z)=f(w)+(f(z)−f(w)).\n\n2. The constant part integrates to 2πif(w), since z=w+ρe^{it} gives dz/(z−w)=i dt.\n\n3. The remainder satisfies |∮(f(z)−f(w))/(z−w) dz|≤2π sup_|z−w|=ρ|f(z)−f(w)|→0 by continuity.\n\n4. The outer integral is independent of ρ, so takingρ→0 gives ∮outer f(z)/(z−w)dz=2πif(w), the desired formula.", "role": "<p>Subtract the constant value and estimate the remainder.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Equality of integrals; continuity at w; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(w)=(2\\pi i)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ntimes the given boundary integral.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(w)=(2\\pi i)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ntimes the given boundary integral.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Equality of integrals; continuity at w; prior exports E1/v1;\nkeep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Subtract the constant value and estimate the remainder.</p>", "Sense": "<p>An integral bound uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">circumference2\\pi \\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nand denominator\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthey cancel.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Split\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=f(w)+(f(z)-f(w))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The constant part integrates to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi if(w)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=w+\\rho e^{it}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz/(z-w)=i</annotation></semantics></math>\ndt.</p>", "<p>The remainder satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\oint (f(z)-f(w))/(z-w)</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz|\\le 2\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{sup} _|z-w|=\\rho |f(z)-f(w)|\\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nby continuity.</p>", "<p>The outer integral is independent of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso taking\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho \\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">outer</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint \\operatorname{outer}</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)/(z-w)dz=2\\pi if(w)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe desired formula.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>An integral bound uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">circumference2\\pi \\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nand denominator\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthey cancel. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: An integral bound uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">circumference2\\pi \\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nand denominator\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthey cancel. Withhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Evaluate the shrinking circle", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Equality of integrals; continuity at w;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-excise-the-evaluation-point-1\">§4.N1 — Excise the evaluation\npoint</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nso the closed disk about w of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies inside\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(z_{0},R)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>On the region between the outer circle and this small disk,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z)=f(z)/(z-w)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis holomorphic.</p></li>\n<li><p>Cauchy–Goursat with its induced boundary orientations gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">outer</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint \\operatorname{outer}</annotation></semantics></math>\nh\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz-\\oint |z-w|=\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nh\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere both displayed circles are individually counterclockwise.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-evaluate-the-shrinking-circle-1\">§4.N2 — Evaluate the\nshrinking circle</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Split\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=f(w)+(f(z)-f(w))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The constant part integrates to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi if(w)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=w+\\rho e^{it}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz/(z-w)=i</annotation></semantics></math>\ndt.</p></li>\n<li><p>The remainder satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\oint (f(z)-f(w))/(z-w)</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dz|\\le 2\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{sup} _|z-w|=\\rho |f(z)-f(w)|\\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nby continuity.</p></li>\n<li><p>The outer integral is independent of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso taking\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho \\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">outer</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint \\operatorname{outer}</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)/(z-w)dz=2\\pi if(w)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe desired formula.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=z^{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}=0,R=2,w=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe formula predicts\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint (z^{2}+1)/(z-1)dz=4\\pi i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlgebraically\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z^{2}+1=(z-1)(z+1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe polynomial term integrates to 0 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2/(z-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nintegrates to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\pi i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For w on the boundary the integrand is singular on the contour, and\nthe excision argument is unavailable. Sense rejects the interior formula\nthere; boundary limiting theorems require a different contract.\nReversing the contour gives the negative of the stated integral.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>For w on the boundary the integrand is singular on the contour, and\nthe excision argument is unavailable. Sense rejects the interior formula\nthere; boundary limiting theorems require a different contract.\nReversing the contour gives the negative of the stated integral.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "0897ac67e01cb6a4f775637043ed3c854725d90fe6b233a5978d7d113fe0d2d7", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of cauchy integral formula, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/\">Harvard\ncomplex analysis: Cauchy formula, argument principle, and Riemann\nmapping lectures</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/cauchy-integral-formula.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/cauchy-integral-formula.tex", "markdown": "markdown/cauchy-integral-formula.md"}, {"id": "CA-02", "slug": "liouvilles-theorem-and-the-fundamental-theorem-of-algebra", "title": "Liouville’s Theorem and the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra", "target": "<p>Prove every bounded entire function is constant. Deduce that every\nnonconstant complex polynomial has a complex root.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import CA-01 and differentiation under its contour integral on a\ndisk:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∮</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(z_{0})=(2\\pi i)^{-1}\\oint f(z)/(z-z_{0})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\ndz. The differentiation is justified by a locally uniform denominator\nbound away from the contour. Use connectedness of C and polynomial\nleading-term estimates; do not import root existence. Also use the real\nmean value theorem on a line segment and the extreme value theorem for\ncontinuous real functions on compact disks.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Cauchy derivative estimate", "proof": "1. For any z₀ and R>0 the differentiated formula applies on the disk about z₀.\n\n2. Its length2πR and denominator modulusR² give |f′(z₀)|≤M/R.\n\n3. The same M holds for every radius since f is globally bounded.\n\n4. Let R→∞; f′(z₀)=0 for every z₀.", "role": "<p>Let a contour radius grow while the bound stays fixed.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Entire f with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f|\\le M</annotation></semantics></math>\nglobally; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>Every derivative of order 1 vanishes.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: Every derivative of order 1 vanishes.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Entire f with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f|\\le M</annotation></semantics></math>\nglobally; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and\nversions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Let a contour radius grow while the bound stays fixed.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A bound depending on R cannot be sent to infinity this way.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe differentiated formula applies on the disk about\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Its length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi R</annotation></semantics></math>\nand denominator modulusR\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(z_{0})|\\le M/R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The same M holds for every radius since f is globally bounded.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\to \\infty</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>A bound depending on R cannot be sent to infinity this way. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: A bound depending on R cannot be sent\nto infinity this way. Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Liouville closure", "proof": "1. For any z,w, consider t↦f(z+t(w−z)) on[0,1].\n\n2. Its real parameter derivative is f′(z+t(w−z))(w−z)=0; real and imaginary parts are constant by the real mean value theorem.\n\n3. Thus f(w)=f(z).\n\n4. This proves Liouville’s theorem on C.", "role": "<p>Use the connected domain to obtain one constant.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Derivative zero everywhere; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Every bounded entire function is constant.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Every bounded entire function is constant.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Derivative zero everywhere; prior exports E1/v1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use the connected domain to obtain one constant.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Zero derivative on a disconnected domain only gives componentwise\nconstancy.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For any z,w, consider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto f(z+t(w-z))</annotation></semantics></math>\non[0,1].</p>", "<p>Its real parameter derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(z+t(w-z))(w-z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nreal and imaginary parts are constant by the real mean value\ntheorem.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(w)=f(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This proves Liouville’s theorem on C.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Zero derivative on a disconnected domain only gives componentwise\nconstancy. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Zero derivative on a disconnected\ndomain only gives componentwise constancy. Recheck dependent nodes\nN3.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Polynomial root contradiction", "proof": "1. Assume p has no zero.\n\n2. Then1/p is entire.\n\n3. Choose R so for |z|≥R the sum of lower-degree terms is at most |a_d||z|^d/2.\n\n4. Thus |p(z)|≥|a_d||z|^d/2 and |1/p(z)|≤2/(|a_d|R^d) outside.\n\n5. On the closed radius-R disk continuity and nonvanishing give a positive minimum of|p|, hence a finite reciprocal bound.\n\n6. Liouville makes1/p constant, whereas it tends to 0 at infinity and is nowhere zero, contradiction.\n\n7. Therefore p has a root.", "role": "<p>Apply Liouville to a hypothetical entire reciprocal.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Nonconstant p of degree d with leading coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_d\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Every nonconstant complex polynomial has a complex root.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: Every nonconstant complex polynomial has a complex\nroot.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Nonconstant p of degree d with leading coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_d\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Apply Liouville to a hypothetical entire reciprocal.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Bound the reciprocal on the compact interior as well as at\ninfinity.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Assume p has no zero.</p>", "<p>Then 1/p is entire.</p>", "<p>Choose R so for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|\\ge R</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe sum of lower-degree terms is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a_d\\Vert z|^d/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|p(z)|\\ge |a_d\\Vert z|^d/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|1/p(z)|\\le 2/(|a_d|R^d)</annotation></semantics></math>\noutside.</p>", "<p>On the closed radius-R disk continuity and nonvanishing give a\npositive minimum of|p|, hence a finite reciprocal bound.</p>", "<p>Liouville makes 1/p constant, whereas it tends to 0 at infinity and\nis nowhere zero, contradiction.</p>", "<p>Therefore p has a root.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Bound the reciprocal on the compact interior as well as at infinity.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Bound the reciprocal on the compact\ninterior as well as at infinity. Withhold this terminal result until its\ngate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Liouville closure", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Derivative zero everywhere; prior exports\nE1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Polynomial root contradiction", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Nonconstant p of degree d with leading\ncoefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_d\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-cauchy-derivative-estimate-1\">§4.N1 — Cauchy derivative\nestimate</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe differentiated formula applies on the disk about\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi R</annotation></semantics></math>\nand denominator modulusR\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|f&#39;(z_{0})|\\le M/R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The same M holds for every radius since f is globally\nbounded.</p></li>\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\to \\infty</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-liouville-closure-1\">§4.N2 — Liouville closure</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For any z,w, consider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto f(z+t(w-z))</annotation></semantics></math>\non[0,1].</p></li>\n<li><p>Its real parameter derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(z+t(w-z))(w-z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nreal and imaginary parts are constant by the real mean value\ntheorem.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(w)=f(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>This proves Liouville’s theorem on C.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-polynomial-root-contradiction-1\">§4.N3 — Polynomial root\ncontradiction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Assume p has no zero.</p></li>\n<li><p>Then 1/p is entire.</p></li>\n<li><p>Choose R so for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|\\ge R</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe sum of lower-degree terms is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a_d\\Vert z|^d/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|p(z)|\\ge |a_d\\Vert z|^d/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|1/p(z)|\\le 2/(|a_d|R^d)</annotation></semantics></math>\noutside.</p></li>\n<li><p>On the closed radius-R disk continuity and nonvanishing give a\npositive minimum of|p|, hence a finite reciprocal bound.</p></li>\n<li><p>Liouville makes 1/p constant, whereas it tends to 0 at infinity\nand is nowhere zero, contradiction.</p></li>\n<li><p>Therefore p has a root.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>The entire function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>z</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^z</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonconstant and is unbounded along positive real z, consistent with\nLiouville. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p=z^{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe root-existence conclusion holds and the explicit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">factors(z-i)(z+i)</annotation></semantics></math>\nillustrate it.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>The function1/z is bounded\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on\\{|z|\\ge 1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut has a pole at 0, so it is not a counterexample to Liouville. Sense\nidentifies the missing entire-domain condition; a bounded function on\nthe unit disk can also be nonconstant.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>The function1/z is bounded\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on\\{|z|\\ge 1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut has a pole at 0, so it is not a counterexample to Liouville. Sense\nidentifies the missing entire-domain condition; a bounded function on\nthe unit disk can also be nonconstant.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "ad8bedd928f1a10d604ebc94400f9cccfc887deb1ceb6b7588fc2cdd80ac7ef2", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of liouville’s theorem and the\nfundamental theorem of algebra, with explicit mathematical contracts,\nlocal verification gates, and reusable exports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/\">Harvard\ncomplex analysis: Cauchy formula, argument principle, and Riemann\nmapping lectures</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/liouvilles-theorem-and-the-fundamental-theorem-of-algebra.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/liouvilles-theorem-and-the-fundamental-theorem-of-algebra.tex", "markdown": "markdown/liouvilles-theorem-and-the-fundamental-theorem-of-algebra.md"}, {"id": "CA-03", "slug": "residue-theorem", "title": "Residue Theorem", "target": "<p>Let D be a bounded Jordan domain whose positively oriented boundary\ngamma is piecewise smooth. Let f be holomorphic in an open neighborhood\nof the closure of D except for finitely many isolated singularities\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_1,\\ldots,a_s</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside D. Then</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\sum_{j=1}^s\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The output is a contour identity with all interior singularities\nincluded. Singularities on the contour are excluded. Essential isolated\nsingularities are allowed; the theorem does not require every\nsingularity to be a pole.</p>", "imports": ["<p>a residue is the coefficient of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(z-a)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the Laurent expansion; positive outer orientation is\ncounterclockwise. Import the Laurent expansion theorem and uniform\nconvergence on compact annuli. Import Cauchy–Goursat’s boundary form: a\nfunction holomorphic near a finitely connected region’s closure has zero\nintegral around its full oriented boundary. This follows by cuts or\nsubdivision into simply connected pieces with cancellation of internal\nsides; it is not the residue theorem being proved.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Construct the Excision Geometry", "proof": "Choose small closed disks around the a_j, disjoint from one another and contained in D, with no other singularity in any disk. Let C_j be the positively oriented circle bounding the jth disk. Their radii can be chosen because the singularity list is finite and each point is isolated.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: Every isolated interior singularity has a disjoint closed\nisolating disk lying in the domain.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Holomorphic domain and singularities</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Choose disjoint local disks</p>", "Sense": "<p>Exclude boundary singularities</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Construct the Excision Geometry. Establish the following local\nresult: Every isolated interior singularity has a disjoint closed\nisolating disk lying in the domain.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A positively oriented piecewise smooth Jordan boundary; finitely many\nisolated interior singularities and none on the boundary.</p>", "export": "<p>Every isolated interior singularity has a disjoint closed isolating\ndisk lying in the domain.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Use finiteness and interiority to choose disjoint small disks.</p>", "<p>Keep their boundaries away from singularities.</p>", "<p>Record the outer orientation and the counterclockwise local-circle\nconventions.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Exclude boundary singularities Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Exclude boundary singularities Recheck\ndependent nodes N2, N3, N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Integrate a Local Laurent Expansion", "proof": "Write $f(z)=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z}c_k(z-a_j)^k$ in the punctured local neighborhood. Uniform convergence on C_j justifies termwise integration. Parameterizing $z=a_j+re^{it}$ yields\n\n$$\\oint_{C_j}(z-a_j)^k\\,dz=\\begin{cases}2\\pi i&k=-1,\\\\0&k\\ne-1.\\end{cases}$$\n\nFor k≠−1 the exponential $e^{i(k+1)t}$ integrates to zero; for k=−1 the integrand times dz is i dt. Therefore $\\oint_{C_j}f=2\\pi i c_{-1}=2\\pi i\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)$.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_{C_j}f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\,\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor each counterclockwise local circle.</p>", "Memory": "<p>N1/E1 and the Laurent expansion on each punctured disk, uniformly\nconvergent on the circle.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Integrate a Local Laurent Expansion.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Check the hypotheses and each step of the displayed calculation.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Integrate a Local Laurent Expansion. Establish the following local\nresult:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_{C_j}f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\,\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor each counterclockwise local circle.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1 and the Laurent expansion on each punctured disk, uniformly\nconvergent on the circle.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_{C_j}f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\,\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor each counterclockwise local circle.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Integrate the Laurent series term by term on the compact circle.</p>", "<p>Parametrize\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=a_j+r e^{it}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand integrate each integer power.</p>", "<p>Only the coefficient of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(z-a_j)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontributes; poles and essential isolated singularities are both\ncovered.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Check the hypotheses and each step of the displayed calculation.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Check the hypotheses and each step of\nthe displayed calculation. Recheck dependent nodes N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Excision Without a Sign Error", "proof": "Remove the disk interiors from D. The resulting region has boundary gamma together with the hole circles in clockwise orientation. Cauchy–Goursat applies because every singularity has been excised. Hence\n\n$$0=\\oint_\\gamma f-\\sum_j\\oint_{C_j}f.$$\n\nThus the outer contour integral equals the sum of the counterclockwise local integrals. An inner circle's orientation is reversed in the region boundary; the minus sign is part of the proof.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f=\\sum_j\\oint_{C_j}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Cauchy–Goursat boundary form</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Remove singularity disks</p>", "Sense": "<p>Track clockwise hole boundaries</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Excision Without a Sign Error. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f=\\sum_j\\oint_{C_j}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1 and Cauchy–Goursat for the region with the disks removed.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f=\\sum_j\\oint_{C_j}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Apply the boundary theorem where\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis holomorphic.</p>", "<p>Inner boundaries are clockwise in the punctured domain.</p>", "<p>Move their negatives to the other side, leaving counterclockwise\nlocal integrals.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Track clockwise hole boundaries Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Track clockwise hole boundaries\nRecheck dependent nodes N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Local-to-Global Assembly", "proof": "Substitute the N2 certificates into the N3 identity. This gives exactly the theorem. With no singularities, the sum is empty and the result reduces to Cauchy–Goursat. $\\square$", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\sum_j\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>All local certificates</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Sum independent local contributions</p>", "Sense": "<p>Include every singularity</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Local-to-Global Assembly. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\sum_j\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N2/E2 for every singularity and N3/E3 for the same contour.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_\\gamma f(z)\\,dz=2\\pi i\\sum_j\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Substitute every local residue integral into the excision\nidentity.</p>", "<p>Check no singularity is omitted or counted twice.</p>", "<p>With no singularities the empty sum recovers Cauchy–Goursat.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Include every singularity Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Include every singularity Recheck\ndependent nodes N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N5", "title": "A Complete Real-Integral Application", "proof": "For $f(z)=1/(1+z^2)$, take the real segment from −R to R followed by the upper semicircle, R>1. The only interior pole is i, with\n\n$$\\operatorname{Res}(f,i)=\\lim_{z\\to i}\\frac{z-i}{(z-i)(z+i)}=\\frac1{2i}.$$\n\nThe contour integral is therefore pi. On the arc, $|1+z^2|\\ge R^2-1$ and its length is pi R, giving\n\n$$\\left|\\int_{\\mathrm{arc}}\\frac{dz}{1+z^2}\\right|\\le\\frac{\\pi R}{R^2-1}\\longrightarrow0.$$\n\nThe real integrand is absolutely integrable: it is bounded near zero and at most $1/x^2$ for |x|≥1. Passing to the improper limit gives\n\n$$\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}\\frac{dx}{1+x^2}=\\pi.$$\n\nA residue calculation alone would not justify this conclusion without the arc estimate and existence of the real improper integral.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E5/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}(1+x^2)^{-1}\\,dx=\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Contour identity and decay estimates</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Separate real and arc integrals</p>", "Sense": "<p>Audit improper limit</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E5/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>A Complete Real-Integral Application. Establish the following local\nresult:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}(1+x^2)^{-1}\\,dx=\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N4/E4 for upper semicircles of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nelementary improper integration.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}(1+x^2)^{-1}\\,dx=\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>The sole enclosed pole is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith residue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/(2i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Bound the arc integral by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi R/(R^2-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich tends to zero.</p>", "<p>Use absolute integrability on the real axis and take the radius\nlimit.</p>"], "exportId": "E5", "gate": "<p>Audit improper limit Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N5: Audit improper limit Withhold this\nterminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Integrate a Local Laurent Expansion", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1 and the Laurent expansion on each\npunctured disk, uniformly convergent on the circle.</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Excision Without a Sign Error", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1 and Cauchy–Goursat for the region with\nthe disks removed.</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N4", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: Local-to-Global Assembly", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2 for every singularity and N3/E3 for\nthe same contour.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N4: Local-to-Global Assembly", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2 for every singularity and N3/E3 for\nthe same contour.</p>"}, {"source": "N4", "target": "N5", "export": "E4/v1", "id": "T5", "activity": "N5: A Complete Real-Integral Application", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N4/E4 for upper semicircles of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nelementary improper integration.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-construct-the-excision-geometry-1\">N1 — Construct the\nExcision Geometry</h3>\n<p>Choose small closed disks around the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\ndisjoint from one another and contained in D, with no other singularity\nin any disk. Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the positively oriented circle bounding the jth disk. Their radii can\nbe chosen because the singularity list is finite and each point is\nisolated.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n2-integrate-a-local-laurent-expansion-1\">N2 — Integrate a Local\nLaurent Expansion</h3>\n<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z}c_k(z-a_j)^k</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the punctured local neighborhood. Uniform convergence on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_j</annotation></semantics></math>\njustifies termwise integration. Parameterizing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=a_j+re^{it}</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>.</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_{C_j}(z-a_j)^k\\,dz=\\begin{cases}2\\pi i&amp;k=-1,\\\\0&amp;k\\ne-1.\\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\ne -1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe exponential\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{i(k+1)t}</annotation></semantics></math>\nintegrates to zero; for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe integrand times dz is i dt. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\oint_{C_j}f=2\\pi i c_{-1}=2\\pi i\\operatorname{Res}(f,a_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n3-excision-without-a-sign-error-1\">N3 — Excision Without a Sign\nError</h3>\n<p>Remove the disk interiors from D. The resulting region has boundary\ngamma together with the hole circles in clockwise orientation.\nCauchy–Goursat applies because every singularity has been excised.\nHence</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∮</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mo>∮</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0=\\oint_\\gamma f-\\sum_j\\oint_{C_j}f.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Thus the outer contour integral equals the sum of the\ncounterclockwise local integrals. An inner circle’s orientation is\nreversed in the region boundary; the minus sign is part of the\nproof.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n4-local-to-global-assembly-1\">N4 — Local-to-Global\nAssembly</h3>\n<p>Substitute the N2 certificates into the N3 identity. This gives\nexactly the theorem. With no singularities, the sum is empty and the\nresult reduces to Cauchy–Goursat.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>▫</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<h3 id=\"n5-a-complete-real-integral-application-1\">N5 — A Complete\nReal-Integral Application</h3>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=1/(1+z^2)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake the real segment from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-R</annotation></semantics></math>\nto R followed by the upper semicircle,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe only interior pole is i, with</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Res}(f,i)=\\lim_{z\\to i}\\frac{z-i}{(z-i)(z+i)}=\\frac1{2i}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The contour integral is therefore pi. On the arc,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|1+z^2|\\ge R^2-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand its length is pi R, giving</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\left|\\int_{\\mathrm{arc}}\\frac{dz}{1+z^2}\\right|\\le\\frac{\\pi R}{R^2-1}\\longrightarrow0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The real integrand is absolutely integrable: it is bounded near zero\nand at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/x^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|x|\\ge 1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nPassing to the improper limit gives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}\\frac{dx}{1+x^2}=\\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>A residue calculation alone would not justify this conclusion without\nthe arc estimate and existence of the real improper integral.</p>", "example": "<p>Take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=(z+1)/((z-1)(z-2))</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|=3</annotation></semantics></math>,\npositively oriented. The two local agents independently obtain</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Res}(f,1)=\\frac2{-1}=-2,\\qquad\\operatorname{Res}(f,2)=\\frac3{1}=3.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>N4 sums them to 1, so the contour integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth poles must be included even though their contributions partially\ncancel.</p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 50%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Interaction</th>\n<th>Evidence transferred</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>N1\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nlocal agents</td>\n<td>Disjoint analytic neighborhoods at 1 and 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Local agent 1\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN4</td>\n<td>Residue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-2</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith simple-pole calculation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Local agent 2\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN4</td>\n<td>Residue 3 with simple-pole calculation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N3\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN4</td>\n<td>Outer integral equals sum of positively oriented local\nintegrals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N4\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\ncaller</td>\n<td>Total residue 1 and contour integral\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\pi i</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>", "boundary": ["<ul>\n<li>Reversing the outer orientation reverses the integral’s sign.</li>\n<li>Higher-order poles still use the Laurent coefficient, not the\nsimple-pole limit formula.</li>\n<li>A removable singularity has residue zero.</li>\n<li>Arc decay must be proved for the chosen function and contour.</li>\n<li>A plot or sampled singularity search does not establish the\nexhaustive pole list.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Export the local Laurent-integral lemma, the excision identity, the\nfinite-singularity residue theorem, and the rational-integral\napplication. These modules support the argument principle and Rouché’s\ntheorem in the problem bank.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>Suppose a branch uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/(1+z^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth poles lie on the contour; the theorem’s contract fails.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Node:</strong> N1</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>State:</strong> STALLED</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failing faculty:</strong> Sense</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failed hypothesis:</strong> no singularities on\ncontour</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Observed:</strong> poles i and -i on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|=1</annotation></semantics></math></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Repair target:</strong> contour selection</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Blocked export:</strong> ordinary residue-theorem contour\nintegral</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Memory retrieves the domain hypothesis. Sense identifies both\nboundary poles. Intellect selects\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|z|=2</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a revised problem. Action checks both poles are interior and\ncomputes residues 1/(2i) and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1/(2i)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose sum is zero. Ego exports integral zero for the revised contour. An\nindented contour or principal value would be a different problem\nrequiring additional analysis.</p>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<ul>\n<li>Reversing the outer orientation reverses the integral’s sign.</li>\n<li>Higher-order poles still use the Laurent coefficient, not the\nsimple-pole limit formula.</li>\n<li>A removable singularity has residue zero.</li>\n<li>Arc decay must be proved for the chosen function and contour.</li>\n<li>A plot or sampled singularity search does not establish the\nexhaustive pole list.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Export the local Laurent-integral lemma, the excision identity, the\nfinite-singularity residue theorem, and the rational-integral\napplication. These modules support the argument principle and Rouché’s\ntheorem in the problem bank.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": false, "sha256": "11661b8667d9d177291b788d713ad2785a0e14c60c221fe84279702eb8b9699e", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of residue theorem, with explicit\nmathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<p><a href=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/\">Harvard\ncomplex analysis, Laurent series and residue theorem lectures</a>.</p>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/residue-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/residue-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/residue-theorem.md"}, {"id": "CA-04", "slug": "rouches-theorem", "title": "Rouché’s Theorem", "target": "<p>For a bounded Jordan domain with piecewise smooth boundary, let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f,g</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe holomorphic near its closure and satisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|&lt;|f|</annotation></semantics></math>\non the boundary. Prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f+g</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave the same number of interior zeros, counted with multiplicity.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import the argument principle: for holomorphic h near a bounded\npiecewise smooth Jordan domain closure and no boundary zero,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∮</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(2\\pi i)^{-1}\\oint h&#39;/h</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the number of interior zeros counted with multiplicity. It follows\nfrom the residue theorem by locally factoring each zero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=(z-a)^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nu with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u(a)\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe domain has positive boundary orientation.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Nonvanishing homotopy", "proof": "1. Set h_t=f+t g for 0≤t≤1.\n\n2. On the boundary |h_t|≥|f|−t|g|≥|f|−|g|.\n\n3. The continuous positive difference has a positive minimumδ on the compact boundary.\n\n4. Thus every h_t is boundary-nonzero uniformly in t; no h_t is identically zero.", "role": "<p>Keep a strict lower bound for the entire deformation.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|&lt;|f|</annotation></semantics></math>\non the compact boundary; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>A uniform boundary lower bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\delta &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: A uniform boundary lower bound\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\delta &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|&lt;|f|</annotation></semantics></math>\non the compact boundary; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Keep a strict lower bound for the entire deformation.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Strict inequality is used on every boundary point.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t=f+t</annotation></semantics></math>\ng for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le t\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>On the boundary\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|h_t|\\ge |f|-t|g|\\ge |f|-|g|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The continuous positive difference has a positive minimum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\delta</annotation></semantics></math>\non the compact boundary.</p>", "<p>Thus every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>\nis boundary-nonzero uniformly in t; no\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>\nis identically zero.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Strict inequality is used on every boundary point. Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Strict inequality is used on every\nboundary point. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Integer-valued zero count", "proof": "1. Define N(t)=(2πi)⁻¹∮(f′+t g′)/(f+t g) dz.\n\n2. Numerator and denominator vary continuously on the compact contour and the denominator is bounded away from 0; hence N is continuous in t.\n\n3. By the argument principle each N(t) is a nonnegative integer.\n\n4. A continuous map from the connected interval[0,1] into the integers is constant.\n\n5. Therefore N(0)=N(1), proving equal zero counts for f and f+g.", "role": "<p>Use continuity in t and integrality.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Boundary lower bound; argument principle; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The number of zeros stays constant along the homotopy.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: The number of zeros stays constant along the homotopy.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Boundary lower bound; argument principle; prior exports E1/v1;\nkeep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use continuity in t and integrality.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A zero crossing the boundary would invalidate the invariant.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(t)=(2\\pi i)^{-1}\\oint (f&#39;+t</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g&#39;)/(f+t</annotation></semantics></math>\ng) dz.</p>", "<p>Numerator and denominator vary continuously on the compact contour\nand the denominator is bounded away from 0; hence N is continuous in\nt.</p>", "<p>By the argument principle each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(t)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a nonnegative integer.</p>", "<p>A continuous map from the connected interval[0,1] into the integers\nis constant.</p>", "<p>Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(0)=N(1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving equal zero counts for f and f+g.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A zero crossing the boundary would invalidate the invariant. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A zero crossing the boundary would\ninvalidate the invariant. Withhold this terminal result until its gate\npasses.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Integer-valued zero count", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Boundary lower bound; argument principle;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-nonvanishing-homotopy-1\">§4.N1 — Nonvanishing homotopy</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t=f+t</annotation></semantics></math>\ng for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le t\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>On the boundary\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|h_t|\\ge |f|-t|g|\\ge |f|-|g|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The continuous positive difference has a positive minimum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\delta</annotation></semantics></math>\non the compact boundary.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>\nis boundary-nonzero uniformly in t; no\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_t</annotation></semantics></math>\nis identically zero.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-integer-valued-zero-count-1\">§4.N2 — Integer-valued zero\ncount</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∮</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(t)=(2\\pi i)^{-1}\\oint (f&#39;+t</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g&#39;)/(f+t</annotation></semantics></math>\ng) dz.</p></li>\n<li><p>Numerator and denominator vary continuously on the compact\ncontour and the denominator is bounded away from 0; hence N is\ncontinuous in t.</p></li>\n<li><p>By the argument principle each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(t)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a nonnegative integer.</p></li>\n<li><p>A continuous map from the connected interval[0,1] into the\nintegers is constant.</p></li>\n<li><p>Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(0)=N(1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving equal zero counts for f and f+g.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">On|z|=2</annotation></semantics></math>\ncompare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=z^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g=z+1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|\\le 3&lt;8=|f|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z^{3}+z+1</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas exactly three zeros\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">inside|z|&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncounted with multiplicity, although no individual root is located.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=z</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(z)=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\non the unit circle, only\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|\\le |f|</annotation></semantics></math>\nholds. The endpoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a boundary zero. Sense rejects the missing strict margin; the\nzero-count homotopy is not admissible.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=z</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(z)=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\non the unit circle, only\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|g|\\le |f|</annotation></semantics></math>\nholds. The endpoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a boundary zero. Sense rejects the missing strict margin; the\nzero-count homotopy is not admissible.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "669f7ed3758e5ead9839798d491352610b7b3f215a7dc707ed6ae76f1b09e1be", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of rouché’s theorem, with explicit\nmathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/\">Harvard\ncomplex analysis: Cauchy formula, argument principle, and Riemann\nmapping lectures</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/rouches-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/rouches-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/rouches-theorem.md"}, {"id": "CA-05", "slug": "riemann-mapping-theorem", "title": "Riemann Mapping Theorem", "target": "<p>For a nonempty simply connected proper domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>⊊</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega\\subsetneq\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_0\\in\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove there is a unique biholomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb D</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z_0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(z_0)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nreal.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use these imported complex-analytic modules: on a simply connected\ndomain every nowhere-zero holomorphic function has a holomorphic\nlogarithm and hence a square root; a locally bounded holomorphic family\nhas a locally uniformly convergent subsequence (Montel); a locally\nuniform limit of injective holomorphic functions is injective or\nconstant (Hurwitz consequence); the maximum modulus principle; Schwarz’s\nlemma; Cauchy’s derivative bound; disk automorphisms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">conj</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi _b(w)=(w-b)/(1-\\operatorname{conj} (b)w)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese supporting results are substantial and are not proved here. The\ntarget mapping theorem is not imported.</p>\n<p>Also use the open mapping theorem and the local inverse theorem for a\nholomorphic injective map (its derivative is nonzero). These supporting\ncomplex-analysis modules are declared imports.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Construct a bounded injective family", "proof": "1. Choose a∉Ω and a branch h(z)=√(z−a).\n\n2. It is injective since equality of h implies equality after squaring.\n\n3. Its image is disjoint from its negative: h(z₁)=−h(z₂) would give z₁=z₂ and h(z₁)=0, impossible.\n\n4. Let w₀=h(z₀); the open image contains B(w₀,r) for some r>0, so it omits B(−w₀,r).\n\n5. Thus q(z)=1/(h(z)+w₀) is injective, holomorphic, and bounded by 1/r.\n\n6. Scale it strictly into D, apply a disk automorphism to make the value atz₀ zero, and rotate so its nonzero derivative is positive real.\n\n7. This gives a nonempty family F of normalized injective maps Ω→D.", "role": "<p>Take a square root, omit an open disk, then reciprocate.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Proper simply connected\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The family of injective maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith value 0 and positive derivative at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonempty.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The family of injective maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith value 0 and positive derivative at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonempty.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Proper simply connected\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Take a square root, omit an open disk, then reciprocate.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Properness supplies a; a branch must be global on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\notin \\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a branch\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z)=\\sqrt{z-a}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>It is injective since equality of h implies equality after\nsquaring.</p>", "<p>Its image is disjoint from its negative:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z_{1})=-h(z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{1}=z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nimpossible.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_{0}=h(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe open image contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(w_{0},r)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso it omits\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(-w_{0},r)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q(z)=1/(h(z)+w_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis injective, holomorphic, and bounded by 1/r.</p>", "<p>Scale it strictly into D, apply a disk automorphism to make the value\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nzero, and rotate so its nonzero derivative is positive real.</p>", "<p>This gives a nonempty family F of normalized injective maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Properness supplies a; a branch must be global on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Properness supplies a; a branch must\nbe global on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRecheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Attain maximal derivative", "proof": "1. Choose a closed disk aboutz₀ contained inΩ.\n\n2. Cauchy’s estimate bounds every family derivative atz₀ by one common finite constant.\n\n3. Let α be the supremum of the positive derivatives; it is positive by nonemptiness.\n\n4. Pick f_j with f_j′(z₀)→α.\n\n5. Montel provides a locally uniform limit F, with F(z₀)=0 and F′(z₀)=α by Cauchy’s formula.\n\n6. It is nonconstant.\n\n7. Hurwitz makes F injective, and the maximum modulus principle upgrades |F|≤1 to |F|<1.\n\n8. Thus F belongs to the family and attainsα.", "role": "<p>Take an extremal sequence with a nonconstant limit.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Normalized family; Montel and Cauchy bounds; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>An injective normalized extremizer F with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(z_{0})=\\alpha &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: An injective normalized extremizer F with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(z_{0})=\\alpha &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Normalized family; Montel and Cauchy bounds; prior exports\nE1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Take an extremal sequence with a nonconstant limit.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A constant limit must be ruled out before invoking injective-limit\npreservation.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Choose a closed disk about\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontained in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Cauchy’s estimate bounds every family derivative at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nby one common finite constant.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the supremum of the positive derivatives; it is positive by\nnonemptiness.</p>", "<p>Pick\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_j&#39;(z_{0})\\to \\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Montel provides a locally uniform limit F, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(z_{0})=\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nby Cauchy’s formula.</p>", "<p>It is nonconstant.</p>", "<p>Hurwitz makes F injective, and the maximum modulus principle upgrades\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F|\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus F belongs to the family and attains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A constant limit must be ruled out before invoking injective-limit\npreservation. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A constant limit must be ruled out\nbefore invoking injective-limit preservation. Recheck dependent nodes\nN3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Force surjectivity", "proof": "1. Suppose b∈D\\F(Ω).\n\n2. Because F(z₀)=0, b≠0.\n\n3. Let r=|b|∈(0,1) and H=φ_b∘F, which never vanishes.\n\n4. Take a holomorphic square root h of H onΩ.\n\n5. Since |H|<1, h maps into D, and it is injective by squaring.\n\n6. Write c=h(z₀); then |c|=√r.\n\n7. The normalized map ψ_c∘h, followed by a rotation, belongs to the family.\n\n8. Its derivative modulus atz₀ is α(1−r²)/(2√r(1−r))=α(1+r)/(2√r)>α because(1−√r)²>0.\n\n9. This contradicts maximality.\n\n10. Hence F is onto D.\n\n11. Its derivative never vanishes by holomorphic injectivity, and the local inverse theorem gives a holomorphic inverse.", "role": "<p>Construct a normalized map with a larger derivative.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Extremizer F; hypothetical omitted\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in D</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>F is a biholomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: F is a biholomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Extremizer F; hypothetical omitted\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in D</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Construct a normalized map with a larger derivative.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The derivative improvement must be strict, not merely\nnondecreasing.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Suppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in D\\setminus F(\\Omega )</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=|b|\\in (0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\varphi _b\\circ F</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich never vanishes.</p>", "<p>Take a holomorphic square root h of H on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|H|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nh maps into D, and it is injective by squaring.</p>", "<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c=h(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|c|=\\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The normalized map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\psi _c\\circ h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nfollowed by a rotation, belongs to the family.</p>", "<p>Its derivative modulus at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha (1-r^{2})/(2\\sqrt{r(1}-r))=\\alpha (1+r)/(2\\sqrt{r)&gt;\\alpha }</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1-\\sqrt{r)^{2}&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This contradicts maximality.</p>", "<p>Hence F is onto D.</p>", "<p>Its derivative never vanishes by holomorphic injectivity, and the\nlocal inverse theorem gives a holomorphic inverse.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>The derivative improvement must be strict, not merely nondecreasing.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: The derivative improvement must be\nstrict, not merely nondecreasing. Recheck dependent nodes N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Normalized uniqueness", "proof": "1. If F and G are normalized, A=G∘F⁻¹ is an automorphism of D fixing0.\n\n2. Schwarz applied to A and A⁻¹ gives |A′(0)|=1 and the equality case A(w)=e^{iθ}w.\n\n3. But A′(0)=G′(z₀)/F′(z₀) is positive real; hence it equals1 and A is the identity.\n\n4. Thus G=F.", "role": "<p>Apply Schwarz to the transition map and its inverse.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Two biholomorphisms with the same normalization; prior exports\nE3/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Existence and uniqueness of the specified normalized\nbiholomorphism.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1: Existence and uniqueness of the specified normalized\nbiholomorphism.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Two biholomorphisms with the same normalization; prior exports\nE3/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Apply Schwarz to the transition map and its inverse.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Dropping the positive-derivative condition leaves rotational\nfreedom.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>If F and G are normalized,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=G\\circ F^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an automorphism of D fixing 0.</p>", "<p>Schwarz applied to A and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|A&#39;(0)|=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the equality case\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A(w)=e^{i\\theta }w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>But\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A&#39;(0)=G&#39;(z_{0})/F&#39;(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis positive real; hence it equals 1 and A is the identity.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Dropping the positive-derivative condition leaves rotational freedom.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Dropping the positive-derivative\ncondition leaves rotational freedom. Withhold this terminal result until\nits gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Attain maximal derivative", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Normalized family; Montel and Cauchy bounds;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Force surjectivity", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Extremizer F; hypothetical omitted\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in D</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: Normalized uniqueness", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Two biholomorphisms with the same\nnormalization; prior exports E3/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-construct-a-bounded-injective-family-1\">§4.N1 — Construct a\nbounded injective family</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\notin \\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a branch\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z)=\\sqrt{z-a}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is injective since equality of h implies equality after\nsquaring.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its image is disjoint from its negative:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z_{1})=-h(z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{1}=z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(z_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nimpossible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_{0}=h(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe open image contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(w_{0},r)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso it omits\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(-w_{0},r)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q(z)=1/(h(z)+w_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis injective, holomorphic, and bounded by 1/r.</p></li>\n<li><p>Scale it strictly into D, apply a disk automorphism to make the\nvalue at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nzero, and rotate so its nonzero derivative is positive real.</p></li>\n<li><p>This gives a nonempty family F of normalized injective maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega \\to D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-attain-maximal-derivative-1\">§4.N2 — Attain maximal\nderivative</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Choose a closed disk about\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontained in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Cauchy’s estimate bounds every family derivative at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nby one common finite constant.</p></li>\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the supremum of the positive derivatives; it is positive by\nnonemptiness.</p></li>\n<li><p>Pick\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_j&#39;(z_{0})\\to \\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Montel provides a locally uniform limit F, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(z_{0})=\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nby Cauchy’s formula.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is nonconstant.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hurwitz makes F injective, and the maximum modulus principle\nupgrades\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F|\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus F belongs to the family and attains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-force-surjectivity-1\">§4.N3 — Force surjectivity</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Suppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in D\\setminus F(\\Omega )</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=|b|\\in (0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\varphi _b\\circ F</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich never vanishes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Take a holomorphic square root h of H on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|H|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nh maps into D, and it is injective by squaring.</p></li>\n<li><p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c=h(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|c|=\\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The normalized map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∘</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\psi _c\\circ h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nfollowed by a rotation, belongs to the family.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its derivative modulus at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha (1-r^{2})/(2\\sqrt{r(1}-r))=\\alpha (1+r)/(2\\sqrt{r)&gt;\\alpha }</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1-\\sqrt{r)^{2}&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>This contradicts maximality.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence F is onto D.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its derivative never vanishes by holomorphic injectivity, and the\nlocal inverse theorem gives a holomorphic inverse.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n4-normalized-uniqueness-1\">§4.N4 — Normalized uniqueness</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>If F and G are normalized,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=G\\circ F^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an automorphism of D fixing 0.</p></li>\n<li><p>Schwarz applied to A and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|A&#39;(0)|=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the equality case\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A(w)=e^{i\\theta }w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>But\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A&#39;(0)=G&#39;(z_{0})/F&#39;(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis positive real; hence it equals 1 and A is the identity.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For the upper half-plane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{0}=i</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(z)=i(z-i)/(z+i)</annotation></semantics></math>\nmaps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nonto D. The Cayley transform has unit-circle boundary values and maps i\nto 0; multiplication by i rotates the disk. Direct differentiation gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(i)=1/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmatching the normalization.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A multiply connected annulus cannot be biholomorphic to D because\nbiholomorphisms preserve fundamental groups. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega =C</annotation></semantics></math>,\na map into D would be bounded entire and constant by Liouville. Sense\nchecks these domain exclusions before attempting the\nsquare-root/extremal proof.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>A multiply connected annulus cannot be biholomorphic to D because\nbiholomorphisms preserve fundamental groups. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega =C</annotation></semantics></math>,\na map into D would be bounded entire and constant by Liouville. Sense\nchecks these domain exclusions before attempting the\nsquare-root/extremal proof.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Version changed contracts and recheck the revised export and every\ndependent node. Diagnostic feedback is not a proof premise.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "419eb92566d722a7d9a0aec67096fea1268ae1fd80da975c1df79a33a480e539", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of riemann mapping theorem, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><p><a href=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/\">Harvard\ncomplex analysis: Cauchy formula, argument principle, and Riemann\nmapping lectures</a>.</p></li>\n<li><p><a\nhref=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~siu/math113/15_riemann_mapping_theorem.pdf\">Harvard\nRiemann Mapping Theorem lecture</a>.</p></li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/riemann-mapping-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/riemann-mapping-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/riemann-mapping-theorem.md"}], "links": [{"source": "CA-01", "target": "CA-02", "label": "Cauchy estimate", "detail": "The differentiated disk formula bounds the derivative of a bounded entire function."}, {"source": "CA-03", "target": "CA-04", "label": "Argument principle", "detail": "Residues of the logarithmic derivative give the imported zero-count formula."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs. No deployed agent execution or formal kernel verification is claimed."};
